Subject: Keep target runtime libraries out of the native linker environment
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Applies-After: ports/patch/gobject-introspection-1.80.1.patch

get_internal_link_flags adds target library directories to LD_LIBRARY_PATH
for the dumper. Passing that modified environment to the native linker makes
it load Fil-C zlib, which has different symbols (compress2 fails). Snapshot
the compiler environment first. Keep the modified runtime environment for
subsequent dumper execution and shared-library discovery. The scanner check
in tests/gi-link-environment.nix deliberately includes the target zlib directory.

--- a/giscanner/dumper.py
+++ b/giscanner/dumper.py
@@ -239,6 +239,9 @@
         pkg_config_libs = pkgconfig.libs(self._packages,
                                          msvc_syntax=self._compiler.check_is_msvc())
 
+        # The linker is a build-platform program. Capture its environment
+        # before adding target runtime paths for the introspection dumper.
+        linker_env = os.environ.copy()
         if not self._options.external_library:
             self._compiler.get_internal_link_flags(args,
                                                    libtool,
@@ -279,7 +282,7 @@
             shell = utils.which(shell)
             args = [shell, tf_name.replace('\\', '/')]
         try:
-            subprocess.check_call(args)
+            subprocess.check_call(args, env=linker_env)
         except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:
             raise LinkerError(e)
         finally:
